{{Quote|I think I've just found out what they're hiding down here. This place isn't a fortress. It's a tomb.|Obi-Wan Kenobi|<ref name="Part IV" />}}
The '''Jedi tomb''' was located inside [[Fortress Inquisitorius]]. While [[Rescue of Princess Leia (9 BBY)|rescuing]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]], [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] encountered the tombs.<ref name="Part IV" />

The tomb held the corpses of numerous [[Jedi]] slain in the [[Great Jedi Purge]], from [[Jedi Master]]s such as [[Pablo-Jill]] and [[Tera Sinube]], to even [[Faris|younglings]] killed in the [[Operation: Knightfall|siege]] of the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]].<ref name="Part IV" /><ref name="Episode III">{{Film|III}}</ref>

The corpses were openly displayed in a hallway in the depths of the Fortress, kept petrified in blocks<ref name="Part IV" /> of crystallized [[amber (material)|amber]].<ref name="Dark Times">{{HomeVideoCite|set=Obi-Wan Kenobi: The Complete Series|featurette=The Dark Times: Villains}}</ref> Similar methods of storing Jedi remains would be used elsewhere by the [[Inquisitorius]], such as with [[Luminara Unduli]] at the [[Spire (Stygeon Prime)|Spire]] on [[Stygeon Prime]].<ref name="Dawn of Rebellion">''[[Dawn of Rebellion]]''</ref> The hallway was secured behind two sets of [[blast door]]s emblazoned with red pairs of [[Imperial crest]]s, accessible through use of [[code cylinder]]s.<ref name="Part IV" />

In [[9 BBY]],<ref>{{KenobiDate|IV}}</ref> while sneaking through the Fortress in search of where Leia Organa was being held, Obi-Wan Kenobi stumbled upon the hallway of dead Jedi. Deeply unsettled, Kenobi informed his ally [[Tala Durith]] over [[comlink]]s of the tomb's existence, going as far as to call the Fortress Inquisitorius in its entirety a tomb.<ref name="Part IV" />

{{Loc-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The Jedi tombs first appeared in the [[Part IV|fourth episode]] of the [[2022]] television series ''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]''.<ref name="Part IV" />

